    {
      "id": "claim_2c1af7e82ca54d80b0585c5bddb5b354",
      "statement": "uploadImage puts objects with ContentType image/webp and CacheControl 'public, max-age=31536000, immutable', then derives the public URL with fixed precedence: CDN_BASE_URL/PUBLIC_CDN_BASE_URL base plus key wins; otherwise a configured S3_ENDPOINT/AWS_ENDPOINT yields the path-style URL endpoint/bucket/key; otherwise the AWS virtual-hosted URL https://{bucket}.s3.amazonaws.com/{key}. Because URLs are persisted at upload time, later CDN or endpoint changes do not retroactively fix stored imageUrl/thumbnailUrl values.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://apps/api/src/services/storage-service.ts#L44-L76",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:db93a66f6f175741a3f9cebef7ea515b9b478eae9f6dde4ce50daebf132aa326:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_f839927ad6a6466889c0bcd4999b4ed7",
      "statement": "The S3Client is built once at module load from fallback chains (S3_ENDPOINT -> AWS_ENDPOINT, S3_REGION -> AWS_REGION -> 'auto', S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID -> AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID, S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY -> AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY, bucket S3_BUCKET -> S3_BUCKET_NAME -> 'forceorg-media') because .env.example documents S3_* names while docker-compose.yml injects AWS_* names plus S3_BUCKET_NAME; either configuration works unchanged, as DEPLOYMENT.md documents the pairs side by side. forcePathStyle is enabled for any custom endpoint and disabled only on the s3.amazonaws.com fallback.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://.env.example#L22-L28",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8487cc27011ee4d892ef5334e91b3aa9c64444151e8972bad5e6f142f9b41224:"
        },
